  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Bound Court Record",
    "overview": "Every surface is part of one litigant's file laid out on a dark desk. Obsidian-navy is the desk; parchment and ivory are the paper; gold is the binding hardware of tabs, pins and the chronology rail; emerald is the mark of something verified. The system's central gesture is disorder becoming date order, so structure is shown as an act of attention to the file.\n\nDensity is that of a working document: full-bleed fields of a single ground, a wide 1400px sheet, generous section breaks, and tight, tabular detail inside the exhibits. The type pairs a heavy-contrast editorial serif with a plain grotesque that stays legible for a tired reader on an old phone. The system is scoped to the CaseIQ site at `sites/caseiq/`; other sites in this workspace need their own record.\n\nThe world rejects the law-firm template: no skyline hero, no scales of justice, no row of boxed service cards.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Full-bleed single-ground fields in obsidian, parchment, ivory, deep emerald and gold.",
      "Paper objects are the only things that cast a shadow.",
      "Gold binds and acts; emerald verifies; red marks a discrepancy.",
      "Gloock at one weight for every heading and figure; Hanken Grotesk for everything read.",
      "Near-square corners, hairline rules, and round pins on a gold rail.",
      "Motion is a single long settle, always fully disabled under reduced motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Ink-Swap Rule",
        "body": "Bright accents stay on dark grounds. On paper, gold becomes Aged Gold Ink and emerald becomes Emerald Ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Discrepancy Rule",
        "body": "Red appears only where something fails to match or fails to validate. It is never decoration or emphasis.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ground-Matched Focus Rule",
        "body": "Focus is a 3px outline offset 3px: emerald on dark, Emerald Ink on light, Record Ink on gold.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Weight Rule",
        "body": "Gloock is set at 400 only, with -0.012em tracking on page headings. Hierarchy comes from size and colour.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Labels, tabs and buttons stay in sentence or title case at normal tracking.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only Paper Lifts Rule",
        "body": "A drop shadow means a physical sheet resting on the desk. Panels, sections, buttons and forms stay flat.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set every major section as one full-bleed ground and change the ground between neighbouring fields; a slim ruled band may continue the field above it.",
